' Service dependencies
' ============================================================

AuthService ..> SupabaseClient
UserProfileService ..> SupabaseClient
CatalogService ..> VenueService
CatalogService ..> RestaurantService
CatalogService ..> CateringServiceApi
CatalogService ..> DecorServiceApi
VenueService ..> SupabaseClient
RestaurantService ..> SupabaseClient
CateringServiceApi ..> SupabaseClient
DecorServiceApi ..> SupabaseClient
VenueService ..> ItemMapper
RestaurantService ..> ItemMapper
CateringServiceApi ..> ItemMapper
DecorServiceApi ..> ItemMapper
FavoriteService ..> SupabaseClient
FavoriteService ..> CatalogService
BoardService ..> SupabaseClient

AuthContext ..> AuthService
AuthContext ..> UserProfileService
FavoritesContext ..> FavoriteService
FavoritesContext ..> BoardService
FiltersContext ..> CatalogService
BookingController ..> SupabaseClient
BookingController ..> Booking
BookingController ..> Event
BookingController ..> BookingItem
MyBookingsController ..> SupabaseClient
MyBookingsController ..> Booking
MyBookingsController ..> Payment
ProviderPropertyController ..> SupabaseClient
ProviderPropertyController ..> EventService
ProviderBookingController ..> SupabaseClient
ProviderBookingController ..> Booking
AdminManagementController ..> SupabaseClient
AdminManagementController ..> User
AdminManagementController ..> ProviderProfile
AnalyticsController ..> SupabaseClient
PayPalButton ..> PayPalProcessor
PayPalButton ..> Payment

SupabaseClient ..> SupabaseAuth

note right of EventService
  The database stores service-related relationships
  with polymorphic columns:

  entity_type = venue | restaurant | catering | decoration
  entity_id   = target service id

  The UML model represents this more cleanly
  with the abstract EventService superclass.
end note

note bottom of ProviderPropertyController
  Combines provider add/edit/delete flows from:
  ProviderProperties, ProviderEditProperty,
  AddVenue, AddRestaurant, AddCatering, AddDecor.
end note

@enduml
